    localIssues: [{ title: "Gulf storms don't stop at the coast", body: "Hurricanes and tropical storms push flooding far inland across Texas — not just the coast. Contractors serving Alvin see their busiest weeks after major Gulf weather systems." }, { title: "Clay soil and flat land", body: "Much of Texas sits on expansive clay with poor drainage. When it rains hard, water pools against foundations and finds its way in — which is why Alvin sees so many seepage and slab-leak calls." }, { title: "Freeze events burst pipes", body: "The February 2021 freeze proved even South Texas isn't exempt. Burst supply lines and water-heater failures remain a top claim driver statewide whenever temperatures drop hard." }],
    popularServices: ["emergency-water-extraction", "flood-damage-cleanup", "structural-drying-dehumidification", "mold-remediation", "burst-pipe-water-damage"],
    nearby: ["dallas", "san-antonio", "austin", "fort-worth"],
    faqs: [{ q: "How fast can a contractor reach Alvin?", a: "Timing varies by contractor and workload, but with 2 ZIP codes covered around Alvin, same-day or next-day response is common. If water is actively flowing, say so when you request help — and shut off your main water valve first." }, { q: "What should I do before the contractor arrives in Alvin?", a: "If a pipe burst, shut off the main water valve. Turn off power to wet areas at the breaker, move valuables and rugs out of the water, and don't use a household vacuum on standing water. Then document everything with photos for your insurer." }, { q: "Does homeowners insurance cover water damage in Texas?", a: "Sudden, accidental water discharge — a burst pipe, an appliance failure — is often covered under a standard homeowners policy. Flooding from rising water generally needs a separate flood policy. Document the damage and ask your insurer what's covered; this is general information, not insurance advice." }],
